libs/

# 压测和发布验证跨越 Gradle clean，报告放到独立输出路径。
/test-output/

# Test byproduct. GreatWallConfig.file() falls back to Path.of("config", ...) when
# FabricLoader.getConfigDir() throws, which is what happens in a bare JUnit JVM. Any
# test that reads or writes the config therefore creates this inside the project root,
# and it reappears on every test run - so it is ignored rather than committed.
#
# Anchored to the project root on purpose: an unanchored `config/` also swallows the
# Java package directory `.../greatwall/config/`, which is where GreatWallConfig.java and
# GreatWallConfigTest.java live. That kept the test file untracked and invisible to `git
# status` for its whole life, and would silently drop any new class added to either
# package. Only the root-level byproduct directory is meant here.
/config/

